  "worked_solution": "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(7-3{t}^{2})),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({t}^{2}+4))\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-\\frac{6t}{7-3{t}^{2}},\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+4}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
